# Mybizz Capital and Media Concept Plan

Mybizz-Live is the company to be registered in the UK
Mybizz is a suite of online business management platforms, the first of which is Mybizz CS Which serves the consulting and services vertical. Others to follow include an e-commerce platform based on medusa.js and the third serves the education and train vertical Allowing clients to build training, education, and courses type businesses

"Front desk assistant" The first ancient site which I am building, and it will be the first member of Mybizz-Agency. It is also the MVP of MyBiz CS

MyBizz Agency is a project group Within Mybizz-Live

## Objective

Raise the capital for Mybizz CS without a loan, and build an audience before Mybizz CS launches on 1 April 2027.

- **Capital** comes from Front Desk Assistant sales: built and released quickly, before any marketing, and sold in person locally and online.
- **The Front Desk Assistant is the start of the Mybizz Agency:** deliverable agents, meaning agents that deliver work, not merely report on it.
- **Audience** comes from social media channels, filled quickly with content and free business-assistance material related directly and indirectly to Mybizz.
- **Mybizz CS stays a standalone app** with its own built-in agents; the Front Desk Assistant is a separate Project in the same business and never becomes a Mybizz CS add-on. It is in fact the MVP for Mybizz CS

## Personal brand

The brand is the founder: a project manager who set up and ran life-support operations in remote places, from the Congo jungle to Antarctica, now building business software with AI.

- **Relatable and personal:** lived examples from remote sites and from the build itself; relatable beats impressive.
- **A personal playbook:** how a remote sites Project manager, not a programmer, builds and runs a software business with AI.
- **Friendships with the audience:** replies, conversations and community, not broadcast only.
- **An ecosystem:** products and services together with the personal brand, which is what earns the money.

## Principles

- **Credo:** simple, secure, robust, fit for purpose.
- **Fast value:** every product gives the user a useful result Immediately.
- **Build and release first:** the first agent (Front desk assistant) ships quickly, then marketing starts while the agents are sold in person.
- **10% product, 90% marketing** once the first agent is out: at least 6 hours a day go to marketing. 14 hour workday.
- **The biggest competitor is indifference:** content must earn attention in its first ten seconds.
- **System agnostic and self-contained:** every agent runs in its own setup, works with any client's systems, and never depends on a client's messy environment.
- **Self-deployable:** a client sets up an agent with a wizard, without help.
- **Free material draws the audience:** business-assistance material and short courses are given away.
- **Adapt, never copy:** take the structure of proven videos (hook, pacing, format), never their words. Emulate content that has gone viral
- **Outreach that keeps accounts safe:** about 20 to 30 personal messages a day per platform, raised only as the accounts mature.

## The four streams

1. **Mybizz agency: the capital engine and the start of the Agent Automation Agency.**
2. **Media: the audience engine.**
   - **Short form** on YouTube Shorts, Facebook and TikTok, under 45 seconds, as text-on-video, video or image carousels; these drive viewers to the long-form channels.
   - **Long form** on YouTube, LinkedIn and Instagram, in three lines: A builds views and subscribers; B pairs content with offers; C builds a community with courses and workshops.
   - **Free material:** a large stream of business-assistance material and short courses, given away to draw the audience.
   - **Topics:** AI, automation, starting and running a business, and making money with AI.
   - **Repurposing:** each long piece is cut into shorts, carousels, posts and AI podcasts.
   - **Faceless and avatar channels** run beside the personal channel.
   - **Community funnel:** YouTube and Instagram lead into a Skool community.
3. **Mybizz pre-launch: the launch engine.**
   - Lead magnets (free audits, templates and checklists) collect a waiting list.
   - A founding-member offer gives early Mybizz clients a reduced price.
   - Mybizz is a standalone app with its own built-in agents.
4. **Later ventures: once Mybizz is live.**
   - **Digital info products and a paid community,** grown from the content and the Skool community.



## Recently discovered tools

Open-source tools, run on Mybizz's own setup wherever possible, with each tool's fit confirmed in the concept design.

| Tool                                                     | Role                                                |
| -------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |
|                                                          |                                                     |
| Hermes Agent (Nous Research)                             | Candidate agent framework for the assistant agents  |
|                                                          |                                                     |
| [Postiz](https://github.com/gitroomhq/postiz-app)        | Schedules posts across every channel                |
| AI YouTube Shorts Generator                              | Cuts long videos into shorts                        |
| [VideoLingo](https://github.com/Huanshere/VideoLingo)    | Subtitles and translates videos for other markets   |
| [Ghost](https://github.com/TryGhost/Ghost)               | Blog, newsletter and the free material library      |
| [OpenSEO](https://github.com/every-app/open-seo)         | Helps the blog and videos get found in search       |
| [REA](https://github.com/morluto/rea)                    | Studies how proven content and products are built   |
| Skool                                                    | Paid and free community, and the short courses      |
| [APEX Agents](https://github.com/EnvCommons/APEX-Agents) | Reference for agent platforms, to study and emulate |

